    <GaugingStation location="Intake" name="Allt Leachdach" number="91802">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Compound weir measuring flows draining the north-eastern slopes of the Ben Nevis massif.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">No drowning due to the steep gradient d/s, but at low flows the nappe in the V-notch is not aerated. The stilling pool is unlikely to be entirely effective at high flows. Freezing occurs in winter. Theoretical rating.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Compound sharp edge weir with a flat 'V' set in a sharp edge rectangular notch (6.7m long).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural regime.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Mountainous catchment, often snowy in winter. The catchment lies on the north flank of the eastward extension of the Ben Nevis massif. Land cover is rough grazing, pasture and bare rock. No significant catchment changes known.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff"/>
        </Comments>
